tension-DeviceDispense.device</td><td>Element `DeviceDispense.device` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `DeviceDispense` is not mapped.\nElement `DeviceDispense.device` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>DeviceDispense.receiver (receiver)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-DeviceDispense.receiver</td><td>Element `DeviceDispense.receiver` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `DeviceDispense` is not mapped.\nElement `DeviceDispense.receiver` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>DeviceDispense.encounter (encounter)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-DeviceDispense.encounter</td><td>Element `DeviceDispense.encounter` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `DeviceDispense` is not mapped.\nElement `DeviceDispense.encounter` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>DeviceDispense.supportingInformation (supportingInformation)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-DeviceDispense.supportingInformation</td><td>Element `DeviceDispense.supportingInformation` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `DeviceDispense` is not mapped.\nElement `DeviceDispense.supportingInformation` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>DeviceDispense.performer (performer)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-DeviceDispense.performer</td><td>Element `DeviceDispense.performer` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `DeviceDispense` is not mapped.\nElement `DeviceDispense.performer` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>DeviceDispense.performer.function (function)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-DeviceDispense.performer:function</td><td>Element `DeviceDispense.performer.function` is part of an existing definition because parent element `DeviceDispense.performer` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `DeviceDispense.performer.function` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `DeviceDispense` is not mapped.\nElement `DeviceDispense.performer.function` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>DeviceDispense.performer.actor (actor)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-DeviceDispense.performer:actor</td><td>Element `DeviceDispense.performer.actor` is part of an existing definition because parent element `DeviceDispense.performer` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `DeviceDispense.performer.actor` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `DeviceDispense` is not mapped.\nElement `DeviceDispense.performer.actor` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>DeviceDispense.location (location)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extens